{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 1423 pushed for review: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1423 (commit dc30f72def).\n\nTDD evidence: behavioural/contract tests were authored RED-first and seen failing for the right reason (NotImplementedError against the seam + 'assert None is not None' for the p6 wiring), NOT import errors. The implementation subagent was held out from the full oracle - it saw ONLY tests/unit/test_det_measurement_provenance.py (happy path); the edge/enum/binding/placeholder/no-judgement cases and the p6 E2E cases were physically moved out of its worktree. On restore, ALL 42 passed, first attempt, no tier escalation. Mutation testing gave the oracle teeth: breaking the nearest-item binding killed 1 test, disabling placeholder detection killed 4, disabling enum membership killed 8. Refactoring litmus passed - renaming three private helpers left all 42 green, so the tests assert behaviour not structure.\n\nPre-flight: make lint clean, make typecheck clean (434 source files), full make test = 10289 passed / 1 failed / 38 skipped in 45m46s. The single failure is tests/unit/grounding/test_coverage_reconstruction.py::test_full_backend_account_is_present, which is PRE-EXISTING on clean origin/main - verified by stashing this entire change and re-running (identical failure). Filed as bug 0ba2-15e6-d8a6-4a2a, linked discovered_from this story. It is unrelated to this work but may turn CI Verified red.\n\nA near-miss worth recording: .gitignore ignores .rebar/prompts/* wholesale and un-ignores each committed overlay prompt individually. The new rubric was invisible to git; committing without noticing would have passed local tests (which read from disk) and then failed in CI with exactly the PromptNotFound the round-2 review predicted. Added the surgical un-ignore line per the documented convention."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785914038475145001,"uuid":"c8859baa-097f-4b4b-aa40-89c863976748"}